# PATH - Command search path

Type `PATH` to display the configured search locations.

## Search order

The current drive/user is searched first. After a local miss, the
configured entries are tried in order. A dollar sign stands for the
caller's drive or user in that position.

```text
PATH B3: A0:
```

This sets the additional search locations to B3 followed by A0.
Use [HELP source reporting](HELP.HLP#finding-a-topic) to see which copy
of a help topic is selected.

## Editing PATH

```text
PATH /A C4:
PATH /D C4:
PATH /DEFAULT
```

The first command appends C4. The second removes that entry. The third
restores the default path.
